# Code owners. Requests a review from the owner when a pull request touches these paths; combined
# with "Require review from Code Owners" branch protection it makes the review mandatory.
#
# TODO(team): a single user owns everything today. With "Require review from Code Owners" and
# "Require approvals" on, GitHub does not let an author approve their own PR, so that user's own
# PRs would block. Until a team exists, either add a bypass for this user in the branch ruleset or
# require a second reviewer (see CONTRIBUTING.md, "Recommended branch protection"). Once a team such
# as @geoknoesis/security exists, replace @fellahst below with it (one search/replace) and keep the
# user as a member.
# Later patterns take precedence.

# Default
*                               @fellahst

# Security-critical modules
/did/                           @fellahst
/kms/                           @fellahst
/credentials/                   @fellahst
/signatures/                    @fellahst
/trust-registry/                @fellahst
/wallet/                        @fellahst
/anchors/                       @fellahst
/observability/                 @fellahst
/contract/                      @fellahst
/trust/                         @fellahst
/common/                        @fellahst

# CI, supply chain and release
/.github/                       @fellahst
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @fellahst
/scripts/                       @fellahst
/config/                        @fellahst
/gradle/                        @fellahst
/build.gradle.kts               @fellahst
/settings.gradle.kts            @fellahst
/gradle.properties              @fellahst
/SECURITY.md                    @fellahst
